<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Russian troops take Sofia from the Ottomans</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a>, Russian forces under General Gurko entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofia">Sofia</a>, ending nearly five centuries of Ottoman rule. The city became the capital of the new Bulgarian state the following year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-19">19 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Edison receives a patent for the phonograph</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Edison's tinfoil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phonograph">phonograph</a> was the first machine able to record sound and play it back. Its first words were 'Mary had a little lamb'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-3">3 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of San Stefano creates a 'Greater Bulgaria'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a>, the treaty created a large autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. The other great powers revised it at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> that summer, leaving lasting Balkan grievances.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-13">13 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Berlin redraws the map of the Balkans</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> recognised the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montenegro">Montenegro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and cut back the large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Its compromises left grievances that fed later Balkan wars.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress of Berlin was a meeting of the great powers chaired by Bismarck in June and July 1878 to revise the Treaty of San Stefano after the Russo-Turkish War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/occupation-of-bosnia-herzegovina">Occupation of Bosnia-Herzegovina</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The occupation of Bosnia-Herzegovina was the entry of Austro-Hungarian troops into the Ottoman provinces of Bosnia and Herzegovina in 1878, authorised by the Congress of Berlin.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/cyprus-convention">Cyprus Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Cyprus Convention was a secret agreement signed on 4 June 1878 between Britain and the Ottoman Empire.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-zanjon">Pact of Zanjón</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Pact of Zanjón was the agreement of 10 February 1878 that ended most of the fighting in the Ten Years' War between Cuban rebels and Spain.</p></div></li></ol></section>
